{"number": 31, "text": "                     Exercises\n\n\n                    Use a word from  the box in the correct form to complete each collocation. Use each word\n            12.1\n                    once only.\n\n                      shine    dark     light up   sunny     lighten    darken\n\n                    1  | could tell Maria was in a good mood by the             smile on her face.\n                    2  The little boy’s eyes              when he saw his daddy approaching.\n                    3  Let’s put some happy music on to                the atmosphere. Everyone’s too serious.\n                    4  My grandparents lived through the                days of civil war from 1936 to 1939.\n                    5  The girl’s eyes               with excitement as she prepared for the party.\n                    6  Mr Garnham’s expression                 as he was told the terrible news.\n\n                    Read  these remarks by different people, then answer the questions.\n\n                       Jason:        in floods of tears. It was such a sad film.\n                     Thomas:   An hour before the match there was already a trickle of vehicles entering\n                               the car park.\n                       Emma:    |had a heated conversation with Alice the other day.\n                    Madeline:   | didn’t think there’d be much traffic today but there was a steady stream of\n                               vehicles on the main highway.\n                         Rob:  Tempers  flared, I’m afraid, and mine was one of them.\n                    Charlotte:  Everyone was pouring out of the stadium as | drove past.\n\n                                                                                                                 |\n                      1         A   AF                                                                   ———\n\n                        Who got very angry indeed?\n                        Who saw a lot of people all at once?\n                        Who had a disagreement or argument?\n                        Who saw a small number of cars?\n                        Who cried over something?\n\n\n            12.3\n                    Put these words in order to make sentences.\n                    1               / embarrassment / burning / were / My\n                    2  city/up/has/in/  capital / flared / the / Violence\n                    3  flowed / The / during / discussion / ideas / the\n                    4  divorce / was / footballer’s / The / publicity / surrounded / famous /a/ by / blaze / of\n\n                    Answer  the questions.\n            12.4\n                    1 What  is most likely to be fiery?\n                       (a) someone’s intelligence (b) someone’s temper\n                    2 Which  is the most typical collocation? a blaze of\n                       (a)temper   (b) glory (c) joy\n                    3 What  is most likely to be heated?\n                       (a) discussions (b) cheeks (c) troubles\n                    4 What  is most likely to flare up?\n                       (a) love             (c) violence\n\n                    Use a dictionary to find collocations using these words in a metaphorical way.\n            12.5\n                    1  bright      2 warm          3 cold\n\n\n                                                                    English Collocations in Use Intermediate    29", "char_count": 3389, "mean_conf": 88.47, "word_count": 402, "words": [{"text": "12.1", "x0": 247, "y0": 371, "x1": 348, "y1": 408, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "T2.2", "x0": 245, "y0": 1002, "x1": 347, "y1": 1039, "conf": 0, "bold": false}, {"text": "12.3", "x0": 244, "y0": 2134, "x1": 346, "y1": 2172, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"text": "12.4", "x0": 244, "y0": 2465, "x1": 347, "y1": 2502, "conf": 94, "bold": false}, {"text": "12.5", "x0": 243, "y0": 2996, "x1": 344, "y1": 3034, "conf": 96, "bold": true}, {"tex